         </div>
         <div type="section" n="2">
           <p>where-upon, deprived of his sacerdotall dignitie, loosing the dowrie in the right of his wife, and forfeiting all his heritages<note xml:id="holland-jc-note-006" type="annotation" n="d">I take it, that he meaneth such inheritances, as are not Testamentariæ, but Legitima: 1. Which when one dieth intestate, fall unto the children first, and for default of them, to the Agnati and Gentiles, i. to the next of kinne, and to the name. These are called with us, the Right heires at common Law.  Vide Car. Sigon. de Judiciis, lib. cap. 4. De antiq. jur. civ. Rom. lib. 1, cap. 7. </note> descended unto him from his linage and name, hee was reputed one of the contrarie Faction<note xml:id="holland-jc-note-007" place="bottom" n="3">  Of Marius. 
