d perfidious prodicion.</p>
 </note> of his.  The rest of his soulderie he caried with better fame and reputation: and at the winning of Mitylenæ, Thermus honored him with a Civike guirland<note xml:id="holland-jc-note-016" type="annotation" n="d">Made of oken branches, or of Ilex, or Esculus, bearing mast, in defect of the Oke for saving the life of a citizen. Although Generals of the field were honoured therewith, in other respects. </note>. </p>
